I’ve dined at Miriam in the West Village twice recently, and each visit has been exceptional. The atmosphere is intimate, the service is warm and attentive, and the entire experience feels genuinely welcoming. But the true heart of this restaurant is the food — and behind it, Chef Sara, who deserves special praise.

For appetizers, I had the Tzatziki and the Hummus, and the hummus, in particular, was the best I’ve ever tasted. For my mains, I ordered the Branzino on my first visit and the Royal Tagine on the second. Both dishes were exquisite — beautifully balanced, full of flavor, and prepared with an unmistakable personal touch.

What really sets Miriam apart is Chef Sara’s culinary talent and creativity. Her dishes are not only delicious but crafted with a level of care, precision, and personality that you can feel in every bite. She is truly the soul and star of the restaurant, and her cooking elevates the entire dining experience to something memorable.

Miriam is an absolute must-try in the West Village, and I’ll definitely be returning on my next trip to NYC.
